      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/31-crayfishes-shrimps-crabs-snails-mussels/uca-vocans-en/",
      "html": "<p>Fiddler crabs live along the border of water and land. During the tide they hide in holes in the sand. At low water they come out of their hiding places and search for food that the water left behind.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/31-crayfishes-shrimps-crabs-snails-mussels/uca-vocans-en/",
      "html": "<p>The males display their mighty claw to impress the females, but this also is used to awe other males. Within the very same species males exist in which the left claw or the right is enlarged.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/31-crayfishes-shrimps-crabs-snails-mussels/uca-vocans-en/",
      "html": "<p>Some males with extraordinarily large claws were recently imported from Thailand.</p>"
    }
